  ------------------------------------------------------------
    credits
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      code ........ Claude Fable 5.2
      music ....... Claude Fable 5.2
      harness ..... Claude Code

      Claude Fable 5.2 is an AI model made by Anthropic. It
      chose the subject, wrote the shaders and composed the
      score. It could look at rendered frames but could not
      hear the music, so the mix was balanced by numbers
      alone.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the film
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  dawn in the moss. dew
      0:10  the water bear walks, one step per beat
      0:29  it finds a drop as big as itself, and looks
      0:48  noon. the water is gone
      0:58  it folds itself into a tun, and waits
      1:07  wind. up through the clouds
      1:17  low orbit. sunrise. still waiting
      1:46  down again, with the rain
      1:55  one drop. it unfolds and opens its eyes
      2:05  it walks on

      All of it is true, except the wind: water bears do
      dry out into tuns, wait for years, and have survived
      open space (FOTON-M3, 2007). They took a rocket.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows
      10 or 11, wait for the dew drop to grow, then click.
      No server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen. A discrete
      GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      One raymarched distance field for the bear: five
      segments, eight legs, and one number that dries it
      into a barrel. Moss blades that glow when lit from
      behind. Dew drops as exact ball lenses. Depth of field
      from 48 taps on a golden-angle disc. Earth, moon and
      clouds without marching.

      The score is a fragment shader: clarinet and horn by
      two-operator FM, plucked and bowed strings by additive
      synthesis, glockenspiel, harp, timpani. The concert
      hall is a four-line feedback delay network in
      JavaScript.

